erpool one day while he was filling  up his car at a gas station some drunks  started to abuse him one of the  attackers took an iron bar and smashed  his teeth in he thought he was getting  killed he went unconscious and woke up  in a pool of his own blood he eventually  went to the hospital to get treated  after the incident he suffered from  anxiety and became very self-conscious  during the late 80s a new music scene  swept across the uk  sean was captured by the wide-eyed  youngsters in psychedelic clothing  partying at raves  during his final year at university sean  was asked by a friend from his economics  class to go to a party in manchester at  the party sean tried ecstasy and speed  for the first time his anxiety went away  and he was making friends with half the  people at the club  the one-off event quickly became more  regular every weekend shawn and his  friends would join a convoy of cars  heading to illegal raves  however he didn't let his new hobby get  in the way of his lifelong dream in the  summer of 1990 after graduating from  university he boarded a plane straight  to arizona  for around six years sean worked as a  stockbroker high pressure telesales with  brokers cursing and screaming on the  telephone he was a fast learner and  excelled as a stockbroker he even had a  whole team working under him and began  earning hundreds of thousands of dollars  a year  on the weekends sean blew off steam by  throwing parties at his apartment he  started buying 50 xtc pills at a time  from a local dealer and gave them away  to his friends  soon he pledged to bring the uk rave  scene to arizona  stockbroking became too much for him  then in 1997 he left his firm and poured  most of his savings into technology  shares  the shares shot up at the height of the  dotcom bubble and shawn's portfolio was  worth more than two million dollars  at the same time he began using his  wealth to organize bigger raves he  became frustrated with the small-time  local dealers so he drove to la to see  what he could buy from someone higher up  in the chain  for a few years sean built up the  infrastructure of his drug dealing  business solely using ecstasy sourced  from la  he hired a team of people and gave them  cars and apartments  but after a while sean was curious as to  where the ecstasy pills were sourced  from he found out that the pills were  coming from a production plant in  holland  so he sent some of his people over to  try and source the ecstasy pills shawn's  mules would carry around 5000 pills at a  time but as they became more confident  the number went up to 40 000 pills per  smuggling mission back then airport  security wasn't as strict as it is today  and they didn't even know what ecstasy  looked like  in one incident one of his drug meals  got stopped by security they took out  the ecstasy pills and asked her what  they were the drug mule said they were  just vitamin pills the security put the  ecstasy pills back in her luggage and  told her to have a nice flight back in  arizona shawn's business was soaring he  earned the nickname the bank of england  and his ecstasy pills were dubbed  english shawns he even gained protection  from the new mexican mafia after  protecting a gang member called g-dog  from the cops sean didn't know it yet  but he was dealing with one of the most  violent gangs in arizona  with a free protection of a powerful  criminal gang and the false confidence  instilled by increasingly regular drug  use shawn got a bit too comfortable his  competitor in the ecstasy market was  sammy the bull gravano a mafia murderer  and former underboss of the gambino  crime family gravano's crew members  attempted to kill sean and many of his  associates one night gravano's crew  members were dispatched to kidnap shawn  from a nightclub to take him out to the  desert to have him killed but luckily  sean's best friend wild man got into a  fight that night and they had to leave  the club in a hurry  after the conflict sean stopped dealing  and gave up his ecstasy business  in 2001 sean fell in love his girlfriend  at the time claudia convinced him to  clean up his act persuaded he began  trading stocks online he thought he'd  gotten away with years of criminal  activity unscathed but unfortunately for  him in arizona police had seven years to  convict him and they didn't require  physical evidence of the drugs  themselves it turned out that police had  been aware of sean's drug business for  years  tapping phone calls and gathering  witness statements  in may 2002 sean was arrested and faced  a 200-year sentence in america's  deadliest prison  the jail was run by sheriff joe arpaio  also known as the angel of death after  serving two years in maricopa county  jail prior to sentencing sean pled  guilty to a sentence of nine and a half  years and was banned for life from  entering the united states he detailed  dead rats in the food cockroaches  crawling in his ears at night gang  mayhem and violence even the guards were  murdering the prisoners  during this time shawn lost about 28  pounds due to the unbearable food  after signing a plea bargain sean was  moved to the arizona department of  corrections the prison was completely  gang controlled fights often broke out  and at one point he even saw an inmate  get beheaded  his first cellmate was a satanist put in  jail for murder he was part of a cult  that drank blood and ate human body  parts his prison guard then decided to  play a prank he moved sean to a new cell  where his new cellmate was a serial home  invader who had been convicted for  breaking into people's homes and  smashing their kneecaps in with hammers  for sean the prison was hell on earth in  his free time sean began to read he read  around a thousand books in just over six  years  with his newfound love of reading came a  desire to write  he began an anonymous blog called john's  jail journal the blog which was sneaked  out and published by sean's visitors  exposed the terrible conditions of the  jail riots stabbings and rapes it  received national media attention in  2007 sean was released from prison he  went back to the uk and moved into his  parents house even at home he received  numerous phone calls from people he'd  met in prison asking him to help  establish a drug importation business to  the uk but sean declined and chose to  start a new life  since leaving prison sean became a  best-selling author and has published a  wide variety of books including one  about the famous colombian drug kingpin  pablo escobar he also gave a ted talk  started a youtube channel and even hosts  a podcast he's also become a strong  proponent against the war on drugs  he tours schools across the uk educating  children on the risks related to illegal  drugs  he also does a lot of charity work for  local communities he's become a changed  man who's completely turned his life  around  from millionaire stockbroker to drug  kingpin what can we learn from sean  atwood's insane journey  it goes without saying that the drug  business is a dangerous one and while  drugs are glorified by pop culture they  can have serious consequences  but one thing we can all learn from sean  atwood is his resilience he has faced so  much adversity in his life from being  bullied at school and nearly beaten to  death to surviving one of the toughest  prisons in america he always found a way  to keep going and never gave up in a  tough situation and by writing books and  giving talks he's able to share his  experience and highlight the dangers of  the drug business  what do you guys think are drugs  glorified in pop culture and should  countries end the war on drugs the  comment section in this one will be very  interesting  if you guys want to support the channel  feel free to check out our patreon well  you'll get access to exclusive content  monthly q a's discord benefits video  scripts and more every dollar will be  reinvested back into the channel yo